From cf2b5cfb84cf4cd6be519a9afc070b8776dc7293 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henning Hollermann <laclaro@mail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:27:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Vero 4K+: keep audio playing below 30 fps, tuning hooks

Audio on slow devices, found on a Vero 4K+ (Mali-450, races at 15-24 fps
at 1080p with gInternalResolution 0.75):

- Audio is generated once per game frame, so below 30 fps the queue ran
  dry and the sound stuttered. The audio thread now generates up to six
  updates per frame until the queue holds the slowest recent frame
  (decaying over ~2 s) times 1.25 plus one device buffer, because SDL
  takes whole device buffers and pads a short one with silence. Music
  and effects then play in real time while the game runs slow; at a
  steady 30 fps nothing changes.
- SPAGHETTIKART_AUDIO_SAMPLES sets the SDL device buffer (default 512 =
  19 ms, which underruns on the Vero; it uses 1024).
- SPAGHETTIKART_FRAME_STATS=1 logs fps, frame time split and the lowest
  queued audio every 5 s.
- libultraship: GLES2 framebuffer/GL error diagnostics, NPOT-safe
  framebuffer textures, gControllers.AutoAssignPorts for one gamepad per
  player.

Summary of the Vero 4K+ port on this branch (OSMC/Debian bullseye armhf,
Mali-450 with OpenGL ES 2.0 only, SDL 2.0.20 mali-fbdev):

- OpenGL ES 2.0 renderer (USE_OPENGLES2) in libultraship and GLSL ES 1.00
  versions of the shaders; no MSAA, VAOs or depth readback.
- Yes/No prompts answer Yes when SDL has no message box support
  (mali/fbdev), instead of exiting with an uninitialised answer.
- Cross-compiled in a Docker image built from the Vero's own sysroot
  (gcc 10.2 / glibc 2.31 to match bullseye), with RUNPATH /opt/vero3/lib
  for the Mali blob; the build scripts and patches live outside this
  repository (spaghettikart-cross).
- Kodi launcher (outside this repository): stops Kodi in a transient
  systemd unit and restarts it on exit, pins HDMI to 1080p60 (other modes
  stayed black), plays to hdmi:CARD=AMLMESONAUDIO exclusively through a
  plug converting to 48 kHz (TVs stay silent at the game's 26800 Hz),
  adds the input group for controller access, and ships an up-to-date
  gamecontrollerdb.txt (SDL 2.0.20 predates e.g. the 8BitDo Ultimate 2C).
- Recommended settings: gInternalResolution 0.75, gTextureFilter 1
  (linear; the 3-point filter is costly on the Mali-450).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
